DPF: state parameters cut at a read boundary (CLAP stateLoad, VST3 setState)

A string that ends exactly at the end of a stream read was taken as complete when the
stale byte after the read happened to be zero, splitting keys and values across reads.
Upstream: not fixed in DPF develop as of 2026-11 (see patches/README.md).

--- a/distrho/src/DistrhoPluginCLAP.cpp	2026-11-25 21:02:30.851234622 +1100
+++ b/distrho/src/DistrhoPluginCLAP.cpp	2026-11-25 21:02:30.872234775 +1100
@@ -1612,7 +1612,9 @@
                 buffer[read] = orig;
 
                 // if buffer offset points to null, we found the end of a string, lets check
-                if (buffer[i] == '\0')
+                // (only within the bytes just read: past them is stale data from an earlier read,
+                //  and a string that runs to the end of this read continues in the next one)
+                if (i < read && buffer[i] == '\0')
                 {
                     // special keys
                     if (key == "__dpf_state_begin__")
